        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "The ligand H2LOMe was prepared separately. For complex 1, a mixture of H2LOMe (0.2 mmol, 0.06 g), GdCl3·6H2O (0.5 mmol, 0.189 g) and Et3N (0.40 mmol, 56 µL) in 20 mL MeOH was stirred for 3 min, then Mn(OAc)2·4H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.049 g) was added. The clear yellow solution was stirred briefly and filtered. Yellow block crystals formed by slow diffusion of diethyl ether vapour into the solution after 3 days. The main text states that the reaction was carried out in MeOH at room temperature and gave a moderate yield; the SI reports ca. 46%.",
